WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:15.978
Peter Wilks' funeral was going to be the next afternoon.

2
00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:20.062
In the meantime, his coffin was in the parlor of his house.

3
00:00:20.982 --> 00:00:25.246
I watched with disgust while the king prayed and cried beside the coffin.

4
00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:31.932
Meanwhile, the duke, who was pretending to be William, just stood quietly and looked sad.

5
00:00:33.284 --> 00:00:36.325
Mary Jane gave the king the letter that Peter Wilks had left.

6
00:00:37.146 --> 00:00:38.106
He read it aloud.

7
00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:43.428
It said that Peter gave his own house and three thousand dollars to his three nieces.

8
00:00:44.689 --> 00:00:50.691
He gave his tannery business, some other houses and land, and three thousand dollars to his brothers Harvey

9
00:00:50.791 --> 00:00:51.251
and William.

10
00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:57.954
The letter also said where the money—six thousand dollars in gold coins—was hidden in the cellar.

11
00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:02.096
Right away, the king and the duke said they would get the money.

12
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.142
They took me with them to the dark cellar and asked me to hold a candle.

13
00:01:08.102 --> 00:01:12.324
They quickly found the bag of money, and their eyes shone with greed.

14
00:01:13.445 --> 00:01:17.126
The two men counted the coins carefully to make sure it was all there.

15
00:01:18.307 --> 00:01:21.948
Then we went upstairs, and they counted it again in front of everyone.

16
00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:25.970
"My friends," said the king.

17
00:01:26.991 --> 00:01:29.772
"My poor brother has been very generous.

18
00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:37.047
He left as much as he could to these poor lambs"—he meant the three girls— "but he wanted

19
00:01:37.127 --> 00:01:39.768
to leave something for us, his brothers.

20
00:01:40.988 --> 00:01:43.890
However, I feel they need it more.

21
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:49.392
Here, Mary Jane, Susan, and Joanna— take it all."

22
00:01:50.172 --> 00:01:52.353
The king handed the bag to Mary Jane.

23
00:01:53.714 --> 00:01:55.815
Everyone said how generous he was.

24
00:01:56.795 --> 00:02:01.773
While the girls hugged and kissed him, I noticed that a tall man had come into the room.

25
00:02:02.994 --> 00:02:07.997
The king noticed him and went over to shake his hand, but the man pulled his hand away

26
00:02:08.117 --> 00:02:16.521
angrily. "Why Doctor Robinson," Mary Jane said, "don't you know this is my uncle's brother Harvey Wilks?"

27
00:02:17.562 --> 00:02:21.064
"He's just pretending to be an Englishman," the doctor replied.

28
00:02:21.884 --> 00:02:24.346
"He has the worst English accent I've ever heard.

29
00:02:25.406 --> 00:02:28.548
I don't believe he is my good friend's brother, and I won't shake his hand."

30
00:02:29.884 --> 00:02:35.206
Mary Jane was shocked, but the doctor continued, "I warn you not to trust these men.

31
00:02:36.227 --> 00:02:39.848
They've learned all about your family somehow, and they have come here to cheat you."

32
00:02:41.149 --> 00:02:45.230
But Mary Jane said to the doctor, "Here is my answer to you."

33
00:02:46.211 --> 00:02:48.672
She took the bag of money and gave it to the king.

34
00:02:48.692 --> 00:02:54.234
"Take this six thousand dollars," she said, "and invest it for us.

35
00:02:54.794 --> 00:02:55.534
I trust you."

36
00:02:56.615 --> 00:02:59.156
Doctor Robinson gave up and left the house.

37
00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.042
That night, there was a big dinner for Peter Wilks' friends.

38
00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:10.727
As a servant, I didn't get a chance to eat until after dinner had been served, but there

39
00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:12.128
was lots of food left over.

40
00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:17.511
I was sitting in the kitchen eating when Joanna, the youngest sister, came in.

41
00:03:18.552 --> 00:03:21.014
She was very curious about my life in England.

42
00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.735
"Did you ever see the king of England?"

43
00:03:24.276 --> 00:03:24.736
she asked.

44
00:03:24.756 --> 00:03:27.698
"Oh, yes," I answered.

45
00:03:27.718 --> 00:03:30.260
"He came to our church every week."

46
00:03:31.052 --> 00:03:33.995
"But I thought he lived in London," Joanna said.

47
00:03:34.015 --> 00:03:35.836
"Yes, he does."

48
00:03:35.856 --> 00:03:38.658
"But don't you live in Sheffield?"

49
00:03:39.279 --> 00:03:41.421
she asked, with a puzzled look on her face.

50
00:03:42.802 --> 00:03:46.685
Darn! I had forgotten that we were supposed to be from Sheffield.

51
00:03:47.606 --> 00:03:48.246
I thought quickly.

52
00:03:48.266 --> 00:03:52.990
"Well, I meant he comes to our church in Sheffield in the summertime.

53
00:03:54.031 --> 00:03:55.712
He comes to swim in the sea."

54
00:03:55.732 --> 00:04:00.156
"But Sheffield is nowhere near the sea," she said.

55
00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.661
"Are you just making this up?"

56
00:04:04.041 --> 00:04:05.541
"No, not at all!"

57
00:04:06.042 --> 00:04:06.782
I said quickly.

58
00:04:07.622 --> 00:04:09.803
But soon I made another mistake.

59
00:04:10.863 --> 00:04:13.504
Joanna asked me how servants were treated in England.

60
00:04:13.524 --> 00:04:17.105
"Oh, very badly," I replied.

61
00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:22.266
"They're not allowed to go to circuses or theaters—or even to church."

62
00:04:22.286 --> 00:04:26.987
"But you're a servant and you said you go to church," Joanna said.

63
00:04:27.007 --> 00:04:29.048
"I don't believe you."

64
00:04:30.712 --> 00:04:33.674
Mary Jane and Susan came into the kitchen at that moment.

65
00:04:33.694 --> 00:04:35.736
"What don't you believe?"

66
00:04:36.416 --> 00:04:37.237
asked Mary Jane.

67
00:04:37.257 --> 00:04:41.200
"It isn't kind to speak that way to someone so far from home.

68
00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.982
You must apologize to Adolphus."

69
00:04:44.902 --> 00:04:47.824
And Joanna did apologize to me, very sweetly.

70
00:04:49.005 --> 00:04:53.108
At that moment, I knew that I couldn't let the king and the duke take their money.

71
00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:58.632
I went up to bed early, but I couldn't sleep.

72
00:04:59.644 --> 00:05:02.566
I had to think of a way to get the money back for the girls.

73
00:05:03.927 --> 00:05:09.211
Everyone else was still downstairs, so I decided I would search the rooms of the king and the

74
00:05:09.251 --> 00:05:14.635
duke. While I was looking in the king's room, I heard the two men coming up the stairs.

75
00:05:15.675 --> 00:05:17.156
I quickly hid under the bed.

76
00:05:18.657 --> 00:05:20.218
They came in and shut the door.

77
00:05:21.239 --> 00:05:25.062
The duke said he thought they should take the money and leave town that very night.

78
00:05:25.082 --> 00:05:27.904
"That doctor might make trouble for us."

79
00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:30.681
But the king refused.

80
00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:37.126
"No, I want to stay and sell the houses and land that were left to us.

81
00:05:38.387 --> 00:05:39.969
We'll make even more money."

82
00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.391
The duke finally agreed.

83
00:05:42.411 --> 00:05:46.334
"But I don't like our hiding place for the money," he said.

84
00:05:46.354 --> 00:05:48.356
"A servant might find it."

85
00:05:49.597 --> 00:05:52.259
The two men got the bag from somewhere in the room.

86
00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:58.344
I heard them making a rip in the mattress just above me, and they hid the money inside

87
00:05:58.364 --> 00:06:02.259
it. Then they went back downstairs to join the other guests.

88
00:06:03.341 --> 00:06:08.191
At that point, although I had no real plan, I quickly grabbed the bag of money.
